  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Global Green Growth Institute CTF</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Programme Purpose: This business case is seeking approval for up to &#xa3;10m of funding towards the Readiness Facility (RF) fund. A &#xa3;4m (approx. $5.3m1) contribution over 4 years would be committed to from the outset (FY25/26) in line with Spending Review period allocation windows, with a review to be undertaken towards the end of 4 years  to assess the need for a potential additional contribution of up to &#xa3;6m.  The RF is one of two pillars of the Global Green Growth Institute&#x2019;s (GGGI) new Carbon Transaction Facility (CTF). The CTF, led by GGGI, will scale up international carbon trading under Article 6 (A6) of the Paris Agreement, while upholding environmental integrity. The RF is a multi-donor fund which will provide technical assistance to support emerging markets and developing economies (EMDEs) in accessing carbon market finance.</narrative>
  </description>
